(33, 'about', 'About Us', 21, '', '', '', '', '', NULL, '', NULL, 'National Acts specializes in VIP Meet and Greet programs for touring artists. Some of our clients include: Testament, Exodus, Cradle of Filth, Death Angel, Armored Saint, The 69 Eyes, Edge of Paradise, Black Satellite, Kataklysm, Ill Nino, Carach Angren, Adema, Julien-K, Through Fire, JR Richards (The original voice of Dishwalla), Austin John Winkler (formerly the voice of Hinder), Sacred Reich, Winger, Warrant, Saliva, Tantric, Rick Monroe and The Hitmen, Allen Mack Myers Moore (Featuring Zach Myers of Shinedown), Soil, Any Given Sin, Death To All, Shallow Side, The Lonely Ones (formerly Bobaflex), and Royal Bliss among many others.<p>\r\n<p>\r\nIn addition, National Acts can provide online ticketing software to midsize concert venues and custom physical tickets for event pre-sales.<p>', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', 1),
(34, 'faq', 'Frequently Asked Questions', 22, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1),
(35, 'terms', 'Terms', 23, '', '', '', NULL, '', NULL, '', NULL, '<p>By using any of National Acts\' services, including any services found on the website, you agree to voluntarily consent to any and all Terms of Service found herein.</p>\r\n                <p>National Acts has the right to modify this Terms of Service agreement at our discretion, and the terms will become effective immediately upon publication to this website.</p>\r\n                <h3>Satisfaction Policies</h3>\r\n                <p>We provide the ticketing software used to process ticket sales and admissions for the events on this website. We are not responsible for the production, experience or cancellation of events on our system. If you are unsatisfied with your experience with an event listed on the National Acts system, you must speak to a valid representative of the event or venue.</p>\r\n                <h3>Status as Content Provider</h3>\r\n                <p>National Acts is not responsible for any content posted or displayed on any page within the National Acts website by our registered clients. Such information does not represent the viewpoints or opinions of our company. National Acts cannot be held responsible for any agreements, contracts, unfulfilled promises or any communication made between one of our clients and a third party. National Acts is not responsible for any illegal or unlawful material â€” including defamatory or copyrighted material â€” posted to an event page by a client on our system.</p>\r\n                <h3>Accuracy of Information</h3>\r\n                <p>Users of any of National Acts services certify that any information provided to us is complete and accurate. National Acts will make every effort to validate the billing information you provide to us; however, if we are unable to do so, we reserve the right to cancel your tickets or prohibit you from using this website.</p>\r\n                <h3>Alteration of Event Listings</h3>\r\n                <p>National Acts reserves the right to expunge any event from the National Acts website at any time, under any circumstances, and for any reason.</p>\r\n                <h3>Refund Policies</h3>\r\n                <p>National Acts is unable to offer refunds after a ticket has been purchased; however, a refund may be issued when an event is canceled.</p>\r\n                <p>If an event is canceled, a refund in the amount of the face value of the ticket will be issued to customers who purchased tickets. Service, delivery and transaction fees will not be refunded. The event promoter will have control over refund availability and duration. National Acts will not be able to issue refunds until any outstanding balance for the refunds has been compensated by the event promoter.</p>\r\n                <h3>Postponed Events</h3>\r\n                <p>If an event is postponed to a later date, it is the clientâ€™s responsibility to update the listing and notify National Acts. In such a case, the eventâ€™s promoter is required to accept outdated tickets at the door for entrance into the event.</p>\r\n                <h3>National Acts Ticket Purchasing Fees</h3>\r\n                <p>Non-refundable service fees may be added to each ticket and/or order. By purchasing tickets from National Acts, you agree to pay these fees and understand that the fees will not be refunded under any circumstances. The customer is responsible for any carrier fees associated with mobile ticket delivery.</p>\r\n                <h3>Acceptable Methods of Payment</h3>\r\n                <p>National Acts currently accepts Visa, MasterCard, American Express (AMEX), and Discover credit/debit cards for payment. All transactions will post a NATIONAL ACTS memo on your billing/bank statement.</p>\r\n                <h3>Privacy Policies</h3>\r\n                <p>National Acts respects your right to privacy. While your email address and purchase information is provided to the business who organizes the event to which you have purchased tickets, we will never share your information with other third parties.</p>\r\n                <p>In addition, we will only use your email address for password retrieval.</p>\r\n                <p>National Acts is not responsible for any personal information posted on this website in a non-confidential manner (i.e. not posted via a secure form), and such information is not subject to the policies above.</p>\r\n                <h3>Refusal of Services</h3>\r\n                <p>National Acts reserves the right to bar any registered client from use of any or all of National Acts\' services at any time, under any circumstances, and for any reason. Violation of any of the guidelines below will always result in such punitive action.</p>\r\n                <h3>Illegal Content</h3>\r\n                <p>Posting or linking to any illegal or unlawful content â€” including defamatory or copyrighted materials â€” on the National Acts website will result in the termination of all services that National Acts provides.</p>\r\n                <h3>Prohibited Content</h3>\r\n                <p>Posting any of the following on the National Acts website may result in the termination, without compensation, of all services that National Acts provides:</p>\r\n                <ul>\r\n                    <li>Any communication that incites or promotes racism, sexism, homophobia, bigotry or physical harm to others</li>\r\n                    <li>Any communication that promotes harassment of others</li>\r\n                    <li>Any pornographic or sexually explicit material</li>\r\n                    <li>Any communication that solicits personal information for commercial or advertising purposes that is not otherwise approved by National Acts</li>\r\n                    <li>Any communication intended to engage others in commercial activities that is not otherwise approved by National Acts</li>\r\n                </ul>\r\n                <h3>Ticket Purchasing Limits</h3>\r\n                <p>In order to discourage unfair ticket purchase practices, clients may set maximum limits for the number of tickets purchased per person. National Acts is not responsible for these limits, nor are we able to circumvent them in any way. Any attempted or actual circumvention of these limits by a customer will result in the termination of any further use of any National Acts services and the nullification of any tickets purchased.</p>\r\n                <h3>Unlawful Ticket Reselling</h3>\r\n                <p>National Acts in no way condones the unlawful resale of tickets. Any unlawful attempt to resell tickets purchased through National Acts will result in National Acts terminating those tickets without compensation, as well as the customer being barred indefinitely from use of any National Acts services.</p>\r\n                <h3>Violation of Terms</h3>\r\n                <p>If you violate any of the terms herein, National Acts reserves the right to terminate your account, bar you from using any National Acts services, cancel any ticket orders and take appropriate legal action.</p>\r\n                <h3>External Links</h3>\r\n                <p>National Acts is not responsible for any content or services provided by any websites outside of the National Acts website. This includes any content posted on the event organizerâ€™s website or on any sites linked from the event pages.</p>\r\n                <h3>Advertising</h3>\r\n                <p>We use third-party advertising companies to serve ads after you visit our website. These companies may use information (not including your name, address, email address or telephone number) about your visits to this and other websites in order to provide advertisements about goods and services of interest to you. If you would like more information about this practice and to know your choices about not having this information used by these companies, you can <span style=\"font-family: Arial, serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">read more on <a href=\"http://www.networkadvertising.org/managing/opt_out.asp\" target=\"_blank\">this page</a>.</p>', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '', 1),
